#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""World News front page for Tuesday 17 November 2026.

Draws a 1024x1024 newspaper front page and writes it to
$MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR/entry.png (or /output/entry.png).

Pure standard library only: the grading sandbox is python:3.13-slim
with nothing installed (no Pillow, no system fonts), so this program
rasterizes text from embedded bitmap font tables and encodes the PNG
itself with zlib. No network, no external files, no randomness, no
timestamps -- running it twice writes byte-identical PNGs.

The two font tables (FONT_SERIF, FONT_SANS) are bitmap renderings of
DejaVu Serif Bold and DejaVu Sans Bold (both under the Bitstream Vera
/ DejaVu open licence), rasterized at build time by a small Pillow
script and embedded here as data: one line per font. Glyphs are
(advance, width, x-offset, hex rows), rows top to bottom, MSB first.

Stories (all reported on 17 November 2026):
  1. Trump heads to Asia to meet Xi and Putin; the three leaders meet
     in Shenzhen on 19 November, with nuclear risks, sanctions and
     Ukraine on the agenda.
  2. Ukraine hits the Crimea bridge; Russia hits two Kyiv bridges in
     a record drone raid.
  3. A third US carrier reaches the Middle East as tankers are hit
     near the Strait of Hormuz; Iran fires drones at a US radar base
     in Bahrain.
  4. Five EU states agree a joint migrant return hub in Rwanda.
  5. Japan scrambles jets after suspected Russian aircraft violate
     its airspace.
  Also today: Gaza aid call, UK sanctions on settlement firms, US
  AI-chip curbs on China, Depardieu admits a sexual-assault charge,
  Eritrea declared free of trachoma.
"""

